@startuml

title PENA-Agent — Component Architecture

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

skinparam component {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
}

skinparam database {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #FFFCE8
}

skinparam cloud {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
}

actor User
actor "Developer / Architect" as Dev

package "PENA-Agent Runtime" {

  component "Runtime Orchestrator" as ORCH
  component "Context Manager" as CM
  component "Ingestion Engine" as ING
  component "Trust Evaluator" as TRUST
  component "Relevance Ranker" as RANK
  component "Summarization Engine" as SUM
  component "Digest Generator" as DIGEST
  component "Observability Writer" as OBSW
  component "Learning Extractor" as LEARN

}

database "Repository Knowledge Base" as KB
database "Observability Artifacts" as OBS
cloud "News / RSS Sources" as NEWS
cloud "LLM Providers" as LLM

User --> ORCH : request digest
Dev --> KB : maintains specs\nreviews context

ORCH --> CM : load grounding context
CM --> KB : read specs\npreferences\nlearning

ORCH --> ING : retrieve candidate articles
ING --> NEWS : fetch content

ORCH --> TRUST : evaluate source quality
TRUST --> KB : use trust rules\nsource memory

ORCH --> RANK : rank relevance
RANK --> CM : use user context

ORCH --> SUM : summarize / analyze
SUM --> LLM : prompt with context

ORCH --> DIGEST : assemble digest
DIGEST --> User : present output

ORCH --> OBSW : emit events\nquality signals
OBSW --> OBS : persist logs\nmetrics\nreports

OBSW --> LEARN : provide observations
LEARN --> KB : write learning artifacts

note bottom of ORCH
The orchestrator coordinates the first executable PENA flow.
Components remain small and testable.
end note

note right of KB
Repository knowledge includes:
- specs
- UML
- prompts
- context
- learning artifacts
- provenance notes
end note

@enduml
